From: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: add snps,keep-roothub-ports-powered quirk

dwc3_host_init() unconditionally calls dwc3_power_off_all_roothub_ports(),
a workaround for NXP boards that need to clear PORTSC.PP right after
switching to host mode so that the xHCI reset does not glitch VBUS. The
workaround assumes the xHCI re-asserts PP once its reset completes.

On the A733 that assumption is wrong: VBUS is supplied by an always-on
external load switch (USB_HOST_EN/PM5), and after the xHCI reset the
root port stays with PP=0/PED=0. The on-board FE1.1S hub (and the
AIC8800 behind it) presents its D+ pull-up - CCS=1, confirmed in
PORTSC[3] - but the port is never powered and nothing enumerates.
U-Boot, which does not run this workaround, detects the hub fine.

Add a DT boolean quirk to skip the power-off for controllers whose VBUS
is externally always on, and set it on the A733 DWC3 node. Document it
in the snps,dwc3 binding. No behaviour change for other platforms.

Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3.yaml |  9 +++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi        |  5 +++++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c                                |  3 +++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h                                |  1 +
 drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c                                | 10 ++++++++--
 5 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
@@ -1407,6 +1407,7 @@
 	unsigned		parkmode_disable_ss_quirk:1;
 	unsigned		parkmode_disable_hs_quirk:1;
 	unsigned		gfladj_refclk_lpm_sel:1;
+	unsigned		keep_roothub_ports_powered:1;
 
 	unsigned		tx_de_emphasis_quirk:1;
 	unsigned		tx_de_emphasis:2;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -1873,6 +1873,8 @@
 
 	dwc->dis_split_quirk = device_property_read_bool(dev,
 				"snps,dis-split-quirk");
+	dwc->keep_roothub_ports_powered = device_property_read_bool(dev,
+				"snps,keep-roothub-ports-powered");
 
 	dwc->lpm_nyet_threshold = lpm_nyet_threshold;
 	dwc->tx_de_emphasis = tx_de_emphasis;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -136,10 +136,14 @@
 	int			prop_idx = 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * Some platforms need to power off all Root hub ports immediately after DWC3 set to host
-	 * mode to avoid VBUS glitch happen when xhci get reset later.
+	 * Some platforms need to power off all Root hub ports immediately after
+	 * DWC3 set to host mode to avoid a VBUS glitch when xhci gets reset.
+	 * On the A733 the VBUS is supplied by an always-on external switch and
+	 * clearing PP here is never undone by the xHCI: the on-board hub keeps
+	 * its D+ pull-up (CCS=1) but the port is never powered (PP=0/PED=0).
 	 */
-	dwc3_power_off_all_roothub_ports(dwc);
+	if (!dwc->keep_roothub_ports_powered)
+		dwc3_power_off_all_roothub_ports(dwc);
 
 	irq = dwc3_host_get_irq(dwc);
 	if (irq < 0)
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3.yaml
@@ -75,6 +75,15 @@
   resets:
     minItems: 1
 
+  snps,keep-roothub-ports-powered:
+    description:
+      Do not clear the PORT_POWER bit of the xHCI root hub ports when
+      switching the DWC3 to host mode. Needed on platforms where VBUS is
+      provided by an always-on external supply and the xHCI does not
+      re-assert PP after its reset.
+    type: boolean
+
+
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 required:
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -927,6 +927,10 @@
 				maximum-speed = "high-speed";
 				snps,dis_u2_susphy_quirk;
 				snps,dis_enblslpm_quirk;
+				/* VBUS is provided by an always-on switch (PM5); the
+				 * xHCI here never re-asserts PP after its reset, so
+				 * skip dwc3_power_off_all_roothub_ports(). */
+				snps,keep-roothub-ports-powered;
 			};
 		};
 
